    "md5": "11faf290f1a1ab7e421b44a2e0100362",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "Sampath Bank launches SME business card\n\nSampath Bank has introduced the Mastercard Business Credit Card, a new financial solution aimed at supporting the operational and cash flow requirements of small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in Sri Lanka.\n\nDeveloped in partnership with Mastercard, the card is designed to provide SMEs with greater financial flexibility, improved expense management and enhanced access to digital payment solutions.\n\nThe bank said the card offers flexible repayment facilities, including instalment plans, customisable credit limits based on business performance, and loyalty rewards on business-related spending. Cardholders will also receive access to local and international promotional offers, enhanced security features and online tools to monitor and settle payments.\n\nCommenting on the launch, Sampath Bank Chief Business Intelligence Officer Darshin Pathinayake said the initiative reflects the bank\u2019s commitment to empowering SMEs with practical financial solutions to support growth and strengthen operational control.\n\nThe bank has also launched the Mastercard Purchasing Card for corporates to streamline procurement and expense management. The solution includes transaction controls, merchant category restrictions, automated bill payments and consolidated reporting features.\n\nMastercard Sri Lanka and Maldives Country Manager Sandun Hapugoda said the partnership highlights Mastercard\u2019s continued commitment to advancing digital payment solutions for businesses in Sri Lanka.\n\nSampath Bank said the dual launch forms part of its broader strategy to deliver innovative financial solutions to SMEs and corporates amid the country\u2019s growing digital economy.\n\nLankan Scout leader Bhanuka Karunaratne first to receive Japan\u2019s Wood Badge\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
