    "md5": "ec366cf0d39cb97bc0e410c5f673e77b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1541,
    "chunk_text": "From the first moment he was elected as a Member of Parliament, steps were taken to acquire a large extent of land for the development of Beruwala town. Accordingly, the Divisional Secretariat, the new post office in Beruwala, the Beruwala Youth Vocational Training Center, four medical quarters, the Beruwala Fisheries Complex and other buildings required for the hospital were constructed on acquired land. He had also acquired more land for the future constructions of the hospital.\n\nIt was he who enabled the first two-storied building to Ariyawansha Vidayalaya for the educational purposes of the Beruwala community. Nearly 50 percent of the buildings of D.S. Senanayake Central College also known as Beruwala Central College were constructed during his tenure. The Education office, Meeting Hall and Century Building are some among them.\n\nIt was he who acquired the land for the playground of the Beruwala Central College amidst many objections and also constructed the two new buildings of the Roman Catholic School near the Beruwala Police Station. The two main buildings of Warapitiya School, the meeting halls of Gnanissara and Aluthgamveediya Balika Vidyalayas, the building of the Pambe School and the prayer hall of the Hettimulla Temple, the Munghena Century School building and the two-storied Duwegoda School, the Walatara and Kalavila School buildings, the Meeting Halls of Al Hambra Vidyalay Naleem Hajiyar Girls\u2019 School and the two-storied building of the Roman Catholic School in Diyalagoda were among his achievements."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-16-islandlk-f5169758",
    "num": "islandlk-f5169758",
    "date_str": "2026-05-16",
    "description": "What Bakeer Markar did for Beruwala",
    "url_metadata": "http://island.lk/what-bakeer-markar-did-for-beruwala/",
