    "chunk_size_bytes": 1963,
    "chunk_text": "The Chinese Train to Vietnam!\n\nWhen Sri Lankans were rushing to train stations to go home to celebrate Sinhala and Hindu New Year on April 14, 2026, Vietnam\u2019s Paramount Leader and President To Lam arrived in China for a four-day state visit. He is referred to as such as he heads the Vietnamese Communist Party and the government. It was his first foreign trip since taking office in early April. A key feature of the trip was to experience China\u2019s high speed rail (HSR) network.\n\nHe began the visit with a HSR trip from Beijing to Xiong\u2019an and concluded the visit with a 2,400 KM rail journey from Beijing to Nanjing. Those who remembered, compared President Lam\u2019s Beijing Nanjing rail trip to Deng Xiaoping\u2019s historic HSR trip in Japan in 1978 shortly before opening the Chinese economy. It was after experiencing the trip that Deng had advised Chinese engineers to develop a similar train in China. As Vietnam is planning its HSR, with assistance from China, to lift its economy to the next level, Lam\u2019s train trip is expected to be a historic juncture.\n\nThe 855 KM Yunnan\u2013Haiphong railway (Indo-China\u2013Yunnan Railroad) was the first rail road between Vietnam and China. It was built by the French colonial rulers (1904 to 1910) to deliver European products to the region and take away natural resources \u2013 minerals, opium etc. \u2013 to Europe. Before the rail road, travel time from Haiphong port to Kunming was approx. 28 days (16 days by boat along the Red River and 12 days overland) (Ref. Indo China statistics). The Kunming \u2013 Hanoi rail road now connects the two countries and the proposed HRS is expected to turn a new page in rail connectivity. Approx. 26 year ago twice a week cross border passenger services operated between Kunming and Hanoi. However, due to landslides there were frequent delays and in 2005 the passenger service on the Chinese section was terminated and most passenger coaches were donated to Myanmar (Ref. Media)."
