    "chunk_size_bytes": 1965,
    "chunk_text": "The 855 KM Yunnan\u2013Haiphong railway (Indo-China\u2013Yunnan Railroad) was the first rail road between Vietnam and China. It was built by the French colonial rulers (1904 to 1910) to deliver European products to the region and take away natural resources \u2013 minerals, opium etc. \u2013 to Europe. Before the rail road, travel time from Haiphong port to Kunming was approx. 28 days (16 days by boat along the Red River and 12 days overland) (Ref. Indo China statistics). The Kunming \u2013 Hanoi rail road now connects the two countries and the proposed HRS is expected to turn a new page in rail connectivity. Approx. 26 year ago twice a week cross border passenger services operated between Kunming and Hanoi. However, due to landslides there were frequent delays and in 2005 the passenger service on the Chinese section was terminated and most passenger coaches were donated to Myanmar (Ref. Media).\n\nThose who heard President Lam have worked with China and India to develop the brand new Hambantota and old Jaffna railroads respectively. Some who saw \u2018Yaldevi\u2019 resuming its journey to Kankesanthurai on May 11, 2026 (Ref. Media) asked if trains can usher peace when \u2018Yaldevi\u2019 resumed trips till Jaffna with Indian support. However, the same people never criticized PM Narendra Modi then for helping to rebuild the northern railroad.\n\nSri Lankans should learn from Vietnam, work with those near and far to develop infrastructure to increase connectivity. That will connect people, prevent conflicts and take the country to the next level. Once Rambo destroyed Vietnam on the silver screen but the Vietnamese are working with China to ensure employment even for Rambo types as tour guides and forest rangers etc. Sri Lankans should take the same approach.\n\nFew countries in the world have railways capable of operating at 4,000 meters above sea level\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marke