    "md5": "0845bba6ff76436dc887925c7f6ba9be",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1942,
    "chunk_text": "CameraLK and Sony unveil Alpha a7R VI\n\nAnushka Gunasinghe (second from left) with a delegation from Sony Headquarters in Japan\n\nCameraLK unveiled the highly anticipated Sony Alpha a7R VI and FE 100-400mm F4.5 GM OSS lens at a regional launch event held in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe event marked a historic milestone for the country\u2019s photography and videography industry, as Sri Lanka was chosen to host the premier regional launch of the groundbreaking new imaging technology, further cementing the nation\u2019s growing reputation within the global creative community.\n\nThe exclusive launch event brought together some of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading photographers, videographers, content creators, and visual storytellers for an immersive evening celebrating creativity, innovation, and the future of imaging technology. Organized by CameraLK, the event showcased Sony\u2019s latest advancements in camera engineering while highlighting the rapid evolution and growing potential of Sri Lanka\u2019s creative industry.\n\nAdding further to the occasion was the presence of a distinguished delegation from Sony Headquarters in Japan, including Koji Sekiguchi \u2013 Head of Consumer Imaging Business, Satoru Yamagiwa \u2013 Senior Camera Marketing Officer, Masaki Yamada \u2013 Product Planning Leader for the Alpha a7R VI, Tatsuru Kikuoka \u2013 Product Planning Leader for the FE 100-400mm F4.5 GM OSS, and Masakazu Yamagishi \u2013 Lens Product Engineer Specialist.\n\nSpeaking about the launch, Anushka Gunasinghe, Managing Director of CameraLK, stated:\u201cWe are incredibly proud that Sri Lanka was chosen to host the premier regional launch of the Sony Alpha a7R VI. This is not only a milestone for CameraLK, but also a proud moment for the entire Sri Lankan photography community. The introduction of this next-generation imaging technology reflects our continued commitment to bringing world-class innovation, expertise, and experiences to local creators and professionals.\u201d"
  },
