    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "1eb2a5727d97a044573ac6fb35278057",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1818,
    "chunk_text": "JAECOO J7 PHEV achieves Five-Star ratings\n\nHayleys Mobility continues to lead Sri Lanka\u2019s automotive sector by combining innovation, luxury, and uncompromised safety.\n\nReinforcing this commitment, the JAECOO J7 PHEV has achieved the highest possible five-star rating in both the 2025 Euro NCAP and Australasian NCAP (ANCAP) assessments, excelling across all key categories, including adult and child occupant protection, vulnerable road user safety, and advanced safety assist systems.\n\nThe JAECOO J7 PHEV integrates advanced structural engineering with intelligent driver-assistance technologies to deliver comprehensive protection for occupants and road users alike. From enhanced frontal and side-impact protection to features such as autonomous emergency braking, cyclist detection, and blind-spot monitoring that responds faster than human reflexes, the vehicle is engineered to support safer, more confident driving in real-world conditions.\n\nEuro NCAP (European New Car Assessment Programme) is the independent vehicle safety authority for Europe, covering the European Union, United Kingdom, Switzerland, and Norway. Its five-star rating system is widely regarded as the global benchmark for automotive safety, evaluating vehicles across frontal, side, and pole-impact crash tests, as well as pedestrian protection and a suite of driver assistance technologies.\n\nAustralasian NCAP (ANCAP) is the independent safety authority for the Asia-Pacific region, conducting assessments applicable to Australia, New Zealand, and other participating countries across South-East Asia, including Sri Lanka. Operating in alignment with Euro NCAP protocols, ANCAP assesses vehicles under the same rigorous criteria, ensuring that safety ratings earned in the Asia-Pacific market reflect the highest international standards."
  },
