    "md5": "488f4ebfc5f54b8fcaa64e9d667915d4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1995,
    "chunk_text": "Prime Lands hands over 43 by the Sea\n\nPrime Lands Residencies PLC recently announced the official handover of 43 by the Sea, welcoming its homeowners to one of Colombo\u2019s most distinctive residential addresses on Marine Drive.\n\nConstruction commenced in 2023 and the development has now been brought to life in full, marking the fulfilment of a commitment made to every buyer who placed his or her trust in the project from the very beginning.\n\nThe handover ceremony that was held recently carried the weight of a promise delivered. The homeowners gathered at 43 by the Sea for an evening of fellowship during which Prime Residences officially handed over the project, setting the foundation for a community by the ocean to begin taking shape.\n\nFor those who had chosen this address years earlier, drawn by the prospect of ocean views, city connectivity and the quality that Prime Lands Residencies is known for, the day confirmed that what had been envisioned had been realised without compromise.\n\nThe development has been conceived around the defining idea of where the city meets the shore, a location where proximity to the ocean is matched in equal measure by access to Colombo\u2019s leading schools, hospitals, commercial centres and cultural destinations. Furthermore, the project was developed in accordance with all the requisite approvals. All the transfer deeds are ready to be executed and the project is completely sold out.\n\nRising ground plus 12 floors on Marine Drive, Colombo, 43 by the Sea offers an exclusive collection of three-bedroom and four-bedroom apartments set against one of the city\u2019s most commanding coastal addresses. Every residence has been designed to draw fully from this setting, with layouts, orientations and finishes that reflect the standard expected of an address of this nature. The result is a development that places its residents at the intersection of two of Colombo\u2019s most compelling qualities, its energy as a city and its openness to the sea."
  },
