    "md5": "bf619ef8dd97f56dbe1582fb8160baf3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "SLIM launches National Sales Awards 2026\n\nFrom left: National Sales Award 2026 Project Chairman Damith Jayawardena, Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing Vice President Events and Sustainability Raji David, Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing President Enoch Perera, National Sales Awards 2026 Deputy Head of Jury Jerome Jayasinghe and Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing Chief Executive Officer Chamil Wickramasinghe\n\nThe Sri Lanka Institute of Marketing (SLIM) has officially announced the launch of National Sales Awards (NSA) 2026, marking the prestigious platform\u2019s 25th anniversary milestone in recognising and rewarding exceptional sales professionals across the country.\n\nThe SLIM NSA has been Sri Lanka\u2019s premier platform for 25 years, recognising individuals and teams that have excelled in sales performance, leadership, innovation and business growth. By honouring the professionals who are essential to the advancement of organisations and the national economy, NSA 2026 continues this legacy.\n\nThe official launch now opens entries for organisations and sales professionals representing diverse industries across Sri Lanka. Top-performing individuals and teams that have shown excellence in their respective fields are urged to be nominated by corporate organisations, CEOs, heads of sales, HR and talent development teams and sales professionals.\n\nThrough its transparent and rigorous evaluation process, which is carried out by renowned industry leaders and experts, the NSA has established a strong reputation over the years as the country\u2019s most credible and prestigious sales recognition platform. In Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate sector, the platform has grown to be a benchmark for professional recognition and career achievement.\n\nSLIM President Enoch Perera stated, \u201cAs we celebrate the NSA\u2019s 25th anniversary, we are pleased to recognise a significant milestone in honouring Sri Lanka\u2019s sales professionals who continue to propel businesses and the economy ahead.\u201d"
  },
