    "md5": "ea640887d3e6ffb59725e3cb54db046b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1674,
    "chunk_text": "Prime Group conducts skill development program for PM\u2019s Security Division\n\nPrime Group hosted a special program at the Prime Minister\u2019s Office recently. The program aimed to enhance the knowledge and skills of all the officers serving in the Prime Minister\u2019s Security Division.\n\nThe programme, conducted by Dr. Krishantha Pathiraja, a respected academic and corporate leader, focused on key areas including communication, public relations, leadership, and motivation.\n\nNearly 320 officers participated, including Deputy Inspector General of Police, Jagath Wishantha, who commands the Prime Minister\u2019s Security Division, and Superintendent of Police, Sumithra de Silva.\n\nPrime Group has consistently supported programs benefitting the country and society. As a private sector leader, the company has since inception, continuously sponsored initiatives to strengthen public service, without distinction between the public and private sectors.\n\nAs part of these series, Prime Group has already extended efforts beyond the Prime Minister\u2019s Security Division, conducting programs with mayors as well as provincial councils and local government institutions to strengthen public service efficiency. Each of these initiatives has been met with resounding success, and Prime Group is committed to continuing the momentum, with similar programs planned to further enhance and improve the nation\u2019s public service.\n\nCommenting on the initiative, Prime Group Co-Chairperson Sandamini Perera noted she is deeply committed to contribute such programs as a way of giving back to Sri Lankan society, the very community whose support has been integral to the company\u2019s success."
