    "description": "OrphanCare and AAA Industries forge partnership",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/OrphanCare-and-AAA-Industries-forge-partnership/273-340994",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1779470666.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-22-dailymirrorlk-46bb147f-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "442af457db7726155830c90411f1cb51",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1690,
    "chunk_text": "OrphanCare and AAA Industries forge partnership\n\nMarshad Barry - Deputy Head Orphan Care handing over the Trust\u2019s Impact Report 2025 to C.M. Noohu \u2013 Director AAA Industries flanked by Abdul Rahman Noohu \u2013 Director AAA Industries (extreme left ) and Azad Zaheed \u2013 Head of Orphan Care (extreme right )\n\nThe OrphanCare Trust has entered into a partnership with AAA Industries (Pvt) Limited, a footwear manufacturer, through which the company will make a financial contribution to OrphanCare on the basis of each shoe sold on selected footwear brands.\n\nThis collaboration marks yet another step in expanding the Trust\u2019s efforts to uplift the lives of orphaned children across the country in line with UNSDG No. 10 Reduced Inequalities, thereby preventing a \u201csecond abandonment\u201d of orphans, a term used to describe the loss of care and support children often experience once they leave institutional homes. Through periodic deposits made directly into individual orphan accounts, OrphanCare brings a unique and compassionate approach to help these young adults transition toward independence.\n\nGuided by Article 2 of the UN Convention on the Rights of the Child, OrphanCare ensures that all orphaned children have access to the programme without any form of discrimination, irrespective of their race, colour, religion, region or ethnicity.\n\nApart from the financial contribution to orphan accounts, Orphan Care Trust has been dedicated to supporting orphan welfare through a range of initiatives including education, vocational training, youth and women empowerment, medical and healthcare assistance, and the creation of job pathways for youth leaving care homes upon turning 18."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-05-22-dailymirrorlk-46bb147f",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-46bb147f",
    "date_str": "2026-05-22",
    "description": "OrphanCare and AAA Industries forge partnership",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/OrphanCare-and-AAA-Industries-forge-partnership/273-340994",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1779470666.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-05-22-dailymirrorlk-46bb147f-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "d25379ee87c46a259d33c34cea8e150b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1590,
    "chunk_text": "Apart from the financial contribution to orphan accounts, Orphan Care Trust has been dedicated to supporting orphan welfare through a range of initiatives including education, vocational training, youth and women empowerment, medical and healthcare assistance, and the creation of job pathways for youth leaving care homes upon turning 18.\n\nWelcoming AAA Industries as a valued Merchant Partner, Marshad Barry, Deputy Head of Orphan Care said \u201cThis generous gesture will help us expand the benefits we offer to all orphans registered under our programme. We are pleased to have AAA Industries on-board as we continue our mission to improve the lives and futures of these vulnerable children.\u201d\n\nAzad Zaheed, Head of Orphan Care, and Abdul Rahman Noohu, Director of AAA Industries, were also present at the formalisation of the partnership, further underscoring the commitment of both organizations to this long-term collaboration.\n\nEstablished with Amana Bank as the founding sponsor, OrphanCare aims to create a nurturing and enabling environment for the orphaned children to thrive and avoid a second abandonment. A notable feature of this initiative is that Amana Bank ensures that every donated rupee directly reaches the intended beneficiaries since all administrative and operational costs are fully borne by the Bank.\n\nTo date OrphanCare has enrolled over 3,200 orphans from 90+ child care homes across the country. OrphanCare recently unveiled its inaugural Impact Report, highlighting the transformative difference it has made in the lives of orphaned children across Sri Lanka."
