    "chunk_size_bytes": 1879,
    "chunk_text": "Samsung retains global No. 1 gaming monitor position for seventh consecutive year\n\nSamsung Electronics has retained its position as the No. 1 gaming monitor brand worldwide for the seventh consecutive year, reaffirming its dominance in a market driven by performance, precision, and immersive innovation.\n\nAccording to the latest data from International Data Corporation (IDC), Samsung secured an impressive 18.9% share of the global gaming monitor market by revenue in 2025. This milestone not only extends its leadership streak since 2019 but also highlights the brand\u2019s consistent ability to anticipate and shape the needs of modern gamers.\n\nAdding another layer to its success, Samsung ranked first in the OLED gaming monitor segment for the third year in a row, capturing a 26% market share. This achievement reflects the growing demand for superior visual fidelity and Samsung\u2019s ability to deliver displays that feel less like screens and more like portals into the game itself.\n\n\u201cAs the No. 1 gaming monitor brand, our goal is to continue leading the market with differentiated innovation,\u201d said Executive Vice President of the Visual Display Business Hun Lee. \u201cStrong partnerships with game studios guide our innovation, while a clear technology roadmap keeps us focused. By expanding our gaming library and broadening platform compatibility, we\u2019re delivering displays that perform when it matters most to gamers.\u201d\n\nOne of those partnerships includes global esports icon Lee \u2018Faker\u2019 Sang-hyeok of T1, whose influence echoes across the competitive gaming world. \u201cIn gaming, the smallest difference makes all the difference,\u201d Faker noted. \u201cBeing No. 1 for seven consecutive years shows that so many of us choose Samsung for a reason. I\u2019m excited to see what innovative gaming technologies Samsung will bring next to help us perform at our best.\u201d"
  },
