    "chunk_text": "One of those partnerships includes global esports icon Lee \u2018Faker\u2019 Sang-hyeok of T1, whose influence echoes across the competitive gaming world. \u201cIn gaming, the smallest difference makes all the difference,\u201d Faker noted. \u201cBeing No. 1 for seven consecutive years shows that so many of us choose Samsung for a reason. I\u2019m excited to see what innovative gaming technologies Samsung will bring next to help us perform at our best.\u201d\n\nLeading the charge is the 27-inch Odyssey 3D (G90XF), a glasses-free 3D gaming monitor powered by advanced eye-tracking technology. It creates depth so natural that gameplay feels almost tactile, as if you could reach into the screen and brush against the action. Supporting this experience is the Odyssey 3D Hub, which is set to expand its compatible game library to over 120 titles this year, including upcoming releases like Hell is Us and Cronos: The New Dawn.\n\nFor gamers who demand visual perfection, the 32-inch Odyssey OLED G8 (G80SH) delivers 4K QD-OLED resolution at a blistering 240Hz refresh rate. With Samsung\u2019s OLED Safeguard+ technology, users can enjoy vivid colors and deep contrast without compromising durability.\n\nPushing boundaries even further, the 32-inch Odyssey G8 (G80HS) introduces the industry\u2019s first 6K gaming monitor. With a native 165Hz refresh rate and Dual Mode capability reaching up to 330Hz in 3K, it offers both cinematic clarity and competitive speed. Enhanced with VESA-certified DisplayPort 2.1 connectivity, it ensures seamless performance across gaming and content consumption.\n\nMeanwhile, the 27-inch Odyssey G6 (G60H) redefines speed itself. As the world\u2019s first 1,040Hz gaming monitor, it delivers ultra-responsive gameplay designed for esports athletes and enthusiasts chasing absolute precision.\n\nSamsung\u2019s continued leadership is not just about numbers, but about reshaping how games are experienced. Each innovation adds another brushstroke to a larger canvas where realism, responsiveness, and immersion converge."
